    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p>Bandits rely on the threat of violence to take whatever they want; they include gang members, outlaws, and mercenaries with no regard for the law. Not every bandit is driven by greed, though: some turn to crime because of unfair laws, desperation, or the threats of ruthless bosses. Bandit deceivers use magic to hide their deeds or to stage dazzling distractions.</p>",
